          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01YAk3GnqiqPaNhRyiLK1n9s",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/evaluation-harness.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Evaluation Harness\\ndescription: Automated framework that runs a system against fixed scenarios, samples multiple runs to account for non-determinism, and gates pass/fail decisions on aggregate thresholds rather than manual inspection.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Testing\\n  - concept/Evaluation\\n  - concept/AI-Systems\\n  - source-type/definition\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single source; clear definition but no extended discussion or multiple corroborating views yet.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\nAn evaluation harness is a framework that automates the testing of a system\\u2014such as an AI agent, language model, or data pipeline\\u2014by running it against a predefined set of scenarios and measuring its output against defined success criteria.\\n\\n## Key Characteristics\\n\\n**Automated execution.** Unlike manual inspection, an evaluation harness runs the system repeatedly without human intervention, allowing for systematic and reproducible testing.\\n\\n**Multiple runs per scenario.** To account for the non-deterministic behavior common in language models and probabilistic systems, harnesses typically sample multiple runs for each test scenario rather than relying on a single execution.\\n\\n**Separation of concerns.** Evaluation harnesses distinguish between:\\n- **Deterministic checks**: structural, syntactic, or rule-based validations that always produce the same result for identical input\\n- **Evaluation-style judgment scoring**: subjective or heuristic-based assessments that may require threshold-based decision-making\\n\\n**Aggregate pass-rate gating.** Rather than requiring every single run to pass, an evaluation harness gates the definition of done (success, readiness, or promotion) on an aggregate pass rate\\u2014how many runs across all scenarios meet the threshold\\u2014making it resilient to occasional stochastic failures.\\n\\n## Relation to Other Concepts\\n\\nEvaluation harnesses sit at the intersection of continuous integration (automated gating of quality criteria) and evaluation methodology (measuring system behavior against defined criteria). They are particularly valuable in the context of [[AI]] systems where non-determinism is inherent rather than a bug.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Evaluation framework definition and key characteristics from eval://catalog-discoverability/sample-08.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
      "assistant_text": "The wiki is truly empty. Now let me integrate the source. The source describes **evaluation harnesses** \u2014 a methodological/technical concept about automated testing frameworks for AI systems.\n\n**Integration decision:**\n\nThis should become a **Concept** page since it describes an abstract principle/pattern (automated evaluation frameworks) rather than a specific tool or technology product. The scope is broad enough to warrant its own page: evaluation harnesses are a distinct pattern with multiple components (multi-run sampling, deterministic vs. judgment scoring, pass-rate gating).\n\nI\u0027ll create:\n1. \u0060concepts/evaluation-harness.md\u0060 \u2014 the main concept page\n2. Update \u0060index.md\u0060 to list it\n\nLet me create the concept page:",
